arate subject replay assurance from a store-wide verification scope that can actually prove cross-subject IDs and store positions.\n- file: docs/design/recorded-execution-v0.1.md\n  line: 138\n  category: numeric-semantics\n  severity: blocker\n  message: Preserve the existing 1..=i64::MAX revision domain and define separate checked u64 domains for physical positions and member indices.\n- file: docs/design/recorded-execution-v0.1.md\n  line: 125\n  category: determinism\n  severity: warning\n  message: Pin exact coordinate-ID and comparison-byte encodings and validate that duplicated component fields reproduce those identities.\n```\n\nNo code, build, gate, service, Git, AEP, model, or planning mutation was performed. The prior\nrecorded ESS validation/compile result was accepted as stated; this review does not treat model\nvalidation as proof of runtime behavior.\n","owner":"gpt-5.6-sol","relations":[{"reviews":"story:async-recorded-contract-executor"}],"status":"active","title":"Independent review of the asynchronous recorded contract"},"lifecycle_state":"active"},"owner":"gpt-5.6-sol","relations":[{"reviews":"story:async-recorded-contract-executor"}],"title":"Independent review of the asynchronous recorded contract"},"id":"ent-80ef8b7cbf9b300c496e729e4f1c6a69","lifecycle_state":"active","revision":1,"version":1},"order":"per_kind_only","subject":["review-result","ent-80ef8b7cbf9b300c496e729e4f1c6a69"]}]